pe of offences reported nationally in 2019')","publisher":"Royal Solomon Islands Police Force","url":"https://rsipf.gov.sb/sites/default/files/RSIPF%202019%20Annual%20Report.pdf","licence":"Unless otherwise noted, copyright (and other intellectual property rights, if any) in this publication is owned by the Government of Solomon Islands.","years":"2019","notes":"Row 'Murder', columns Honiara City, Guadalcanal, Malaita, Western, Isabel, Choiseul, Central Province, Makira, Temotu, Renbel, Total. PDF downloaded with curl, pdftotext -layout; the province values sum to the published total (9)."}},"dict":{"b":["Total"],"m":["Murder (offences reported to police)"],"u":["count"],"s":["rsipf_ar_2019"],"c":["2019"]},"problems":"# Solomon Islands - problems and notes\n\n- Only one year found: RSIPF Annual Report 2019 has a table of reported offences by province (Honiara City + 9 provinces) with a \"Murder\" row (total 9). The text notes that RSIPF \"recorded less numbers in major offences including ... 9 murders ... This was a result of the lengthy periods taken to investigate major offences and the processes of case finalisations\", so the count may be incomplete.\n- Malaita, the most populous province, shows only 18 offences of any kind. The report says HF radio roll-out \"will address the long time issue of effective and accurate crime reporting\" in the provinces. Low provincial figures are likely to reflect under-reporting.\n- Other years: tried RSIPF annual-report URLs for 2017, 2018 and 2020-2024 using the same file-name pattern; all came back as HTML, not PDFs. The rsipf.gov.sb \"?q=reports\" page and the 2020 crime-statistics media release PDF (20201224) came back empty or as HTML pages when fetched by direct download. Worth retrying in a browser.\n- Not checked: Solomon Islands National Statistics Office; Ministry of Health deaths by province.","unmatched":1,"shapes":{"shapes_ADM1.geojson":{"source":"geoBoundaries gbOpen SLB ADM1","url":"https://github.com/wmgeolab/geoBoundaries/raw/9469f09/releaseData/gbOpen/SLB/ADM1/geoBoundaries-SLB-ADM1.geojson","licence":"Public Domain","year":"2021"}},"bsrc":{"gb_SLB_ADM1":{"name":"geoBoundaries gbOpen SLB ADM1 (2021), original source: Natural Earth","publisher":"geoBoundaries (William & Mary geoLab)","url":"https://www.geoboundaries.org/api/current/gbOpen/SLB/ADM1/","licence":"Public Domain","read_on":"2026-10-19"}}}